An IIF nested inside another IIF's parentheses fires diag.nested_iif
(info, on the inner IIF), once per nested call however deep: three
levels give two findings. Matching is case-insensitive (iif).
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE Grade;
	:PARAMETERS nScore;
	:DECLARE sGrade;
	sGrade := IIF(nScore >= 90, "A", IIF(nScore >= 75, "B", iif(nScore >= 50, "C", "F")));
	:RETURN sGrade;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE Grade;
	:PARAMETERS nScore;
	:DECLARE sGrade;
	sGrade := IIf(nScore >= 90, "A", IIf(nScore >= 75, "B", IIf(nScore >= 50, "C", "F")));
	:RETURN sGrade;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
4:35-4:38 info nested_iif: Nested IIF() reduces readability. Consider using :BEGINCASE/:CASE or :IF/:ELSE instead.
4:58-4:61 info nested_iif: Nested IIF() reduces readability. Consider using :BEGINCASE/:CASE or :IF/:ELSE instead.
